<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><gpx version="1.1" creator="The Gunks Gravel Escape" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><metadata><name>Awosting Falls &amp; Lake Minnewaska</name><desc>32.9 mi and about 2,400 ft of climbing. Just beyond Awosting Falls, take Scenic Sunset to Lake Minnewaska. Circle the lake and return through the Trapps to Water Street Market. This saves 15.2 mi and skips Lake Awosting, Castle Point and Hamilton Point.</desc><link href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"><text>OpenStreetMap linework</text></link><link href="https://www.mohonk.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Bike-Map-2024.pdf"><text>Designated ridge bicycle routes</text></link><link href="https://www.openspaceinstitute.org/where/new-york/shawangunks/river-to-ridge-trail"><text>River-to-Ridge map</text></link><link href="https://www.mohonk.com/recreation-activities/mountain-biking/"><text>Mountain House carriage roads</text></link><link href="https://www.openspaceinstitute.org/news/lake-awosting-restoration"><text>Lake Awosting loop reopening</text></link><link href="https://parks.ny.gov/visit/state-parks/minnewaska-state-park-preserve"><text>Minnewaska map and cycling conditions</text></link><link href="https://www.mohonkpreserve.org/plan-your-visit/"><text>Cycling day pass and hours</text></link><link href="https://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php?lat=41.736&amp;lon=-74.197"><text>Current point forecast</text></link><link href="https://511ny.org/"><text>Road incidents and traffic</text></link><link href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"><text>How the ride was measured</text></link><link href="https://data.usgs.gov/datacatalog/data/USGS%3A3a81321b-c153-416f-98b7-cc8e5f0e17c3"><text>Elevation estimates</text></link></metadata><wpt lat="41.74685" lon="-74.089171"><name>1. New Paltz · Water Street Market start</name><desc>Start on the north side of Main Street at the rail-trail crossing. Walk west on the sidewalk toward the Wallkill River.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.746712" lon="-74.089882"><name>2. Water Street crosswalk</name><desc>Walk across Water Street in the crosswalk. Follow the north sidewalk onto the separated bridge path.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.746844" lon="-74.090867"><name>3. Carmine Liberta Bridge · west bank</name><desc>At the west end of the bridge, turn north onto the River-to-Ridge path beside the Wallkill River.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.750376" lon="-74.095296"><name>4. Springtown Road · outbound crossing</name><desc>Cross the road at the trailhead and continue west into the fields.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.748664" lon="-74.109195"><name>5. River-to-Ridge field fork</name><desc>Follow the northern branch of the field loop toward Butterville Road.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.752119" lon="-74.123434"><name>6. Butterville Road · outbound crossing</name><desc>Yield at the marked crossing and continue toward Pine Road.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.751247" lon="-74.124877"><name>7. Pine Road · outbound crossing</name><desc>Cross Pine Road and follow the signed River-to-Ridge route to the Foothills. Follow any posted construction controls.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.745812" lon="-74.129735"><name>8. Foothills · east to the Gateway</name><desc>Turn east onto Lenape Lane toward the stone Testimonial Gateway. The route returns to this junction after the pass stop.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.744979" lon="-74.118505"><name>9. Testimonial Gateway · cycling pass</name><desc>The bike track turns at the arch. Walk the signed footpath to the trailhead booth for today&#39;s cycling pass and the Mountain House waiver. Return west on the Pin Oak Allée.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.745812" lon="-74.129735"><name>10. Foothills · uphill on Lenape</name><desc>Continue west on Lenape Lane and climb to the Lower Duck Pond Road junction.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.754881" lon="-74.138625"><name>11. Lower Duck Pond Road</name><desc>Leave Lenape Lane and take Lower Duck Pond Road toward the pond. Follow the bicycle carriage road along the water.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.753538" lon="-74.145161"><name>12. Duck Pond · Glory Hill Road</name><desc>From the northwest side of the pond, take Glory Hill Road toward Oakwood Drive.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.751899" lon="-74.150745"><name>13. Oakwood Drive · climb to the bridge</name><desc>Leave Glory Hill Road for Oakwood Drive. Follow it west to Rhododendron Bridge.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.758328" lon="-74.165507"><name>14. Rhododendron Bridge · Overcliff outbound</name><desc>Cross the small bridge and take Overcliff Carriage Road southwest toward Trapps Bridge.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.737013" lon="-74.194011"><name>15. Trapps Bridge · cross above US 44/NY 55</name><desc>Cross the pedestrian and bicycle bridge. Follow Trapps Road west to Lyons Road.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.73513" lon="-74.218834"><name>16. Lyons Road · cross to Minnewaska</name><desc>Cross the paved public road and continue onto Awosting Falls Carriage Road. The return crosses here again.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.734277" lon="-74.237454"><name>17. Awosting Falls</name><desc>Stop at the signed falls viewpoint. Continue on the carriage road to the paved park entrance drive.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.734173" lon="-74.23863"><name>18. Short route · Scenic Sunset</name><desc>Walk across the park entrance drive and take the orange Scenic Sunset Carriage Road uphill. The long route branches north over the park-drive bridge.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.728068" lon="-74.237296"><name>19. Lake Minnewaska · begin lake circuit</name><desc>Take the red Lake Minnewaska carriage road along the west shore. Return to this junction after circling the lake.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.727451" lon="-74.238259"><name>20. West shore / Upper Awosting</name><desc>Stay on the red lakeside road past the turn for Upper Awosting.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.725422" lon="-74.237643"><name>21. Castle Point junction · stay at the lake</name><desc>Follow the red lake circuit where the blue Castle Point road branches uphill.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.721679" lon="-74.234603"><name>22. Lake Minnewaska · eastern shore</name><desc>Follow the red lake carriage road north along the east shore toward the visitor center.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.729441" lon="-74.235017"><name>23. Visitor-center junction</name><desc>Stay on the short bicycle carriage-road link toward Scenic Sunset.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.728068" lon="-74.237296"><name>24. Scenic Sunset · descent</name><desc>Leave the lake and descend the orange Scenic Sunset Carriage Road to the park entrance drive.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.734133" lon="-74.238627"><name>25. Park entrance drive · return crossing</name><desc>Walk across the drive and rejoin Awosting Falls Carriage Road eastbound. Pass the falls on the way back to Lyons Road.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.73513" lon="-74.218834"><name>26. Lyons Road · cross back to Mohonk</name><desc>Cross Lyons Road onto the gravel Trapps carriage road. Follow it east to Trapps Bridge.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.737013" lon="-74.194011"><name>27. Trapps Bridge · Undercliff return</name><desc>After crossing the bridge over US 44/NY 55, take Undercliff Carriage Road beneath the climbing cliffs.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.758328" lon="-74.165507"><name>28. Rhododendron Bridge · return</name><desc>At the end of Undercliff cross Rhododendron Bridge and descend on Oakwood Drive. Stay on Oakwood at the Glory Hill junction to reach Lenape Lane.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.764665" lon="-74.140982"><name>29. Lenape Lane · descend to the fields</name><desc>Turn south and downhill on Lenape Lane to the Foothills junction.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.745812" lon="-74.129735"><name>30. Foothills · River-to-Ridge return</name><desc>Leave Lenape Lane and take River-to-Ridge northeast across the fields toward New Paltz.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.751247" lon="-74.124877"><name>31. Pine Road · return crossing</name><desc>Cross Pine Road toward the farm fields and Butterville Road. Follow posted construction controls.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.752119" lon="-74.123434"><name>32. Butterville Road · return crossing</name><desc>Cross the paved road on the field trail toward the Wallkill River.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.751616" lon="-74.118573"><name>33. Southern field branch</name><desc>Take the southern branch of the field loop heading east. The branches meet again before Springtown Road.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.750376" lon="-74.095296"><name>34. Springtown Road · return crossing</name><desc>Cross toward the river and follow the riverside path south to the bridge.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.746844" lon="-74.090867"><name>35. Carmine Liberta Bridge · eastbound</name><desc>Use the separated bridge path into town. Walk the short sidewalk and use the Water Street crosswalk.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="41.74685" lon="-74.089171"><name>36. New Paltz · Water Street Market finish</name><desc>Finish on the north sidewalk at Main Street and the Wallkill Valley Rail Trail, at the same point where you started.</desc></wpt><trk><name>Awosting Falls &amp; Lake Minnewaska</name><trkseg><trkpt lat="41.74685" lon="-74.089171"/><trkpt lat="41.746828" lon="-74.08925"/><trkpt lat="41.74671" lon="-74.089777"/><trkpt lat="41.746701" lon="-74.089844"/><trkpt lat="41.746712" lon="-74.089882"/><trkpt lat="41.746716" lon="-74.089991"/><trkpt lat="41.746718" lon="-74.090071"/><trkpt lat="41.746721" lon="-74.090085"/><trkpt lat="41.746744" lon="-74.090217"/><trkpt lat="41.746844" lon="-74.090867"/><trkpt lat="41.74685" lon="-74.090895"/><trkpt lat="41.746864" lon="-74.090922"/><trkpt lat="41.746887" lon="-74.090954"/><trkpt lat="41.746904" lon="-74.090987"/><trkpt lat="41.746922" lon="-74.091036"/><trkpt lat="41.746961" lon="-74.091164"/><trkpt lat="41.746986" lon="-74.091234"/><trkpt lat="41.747025" lon="-74.091338"/><trkpt lat="41.747113" lon="-74.091546"/><trkpt lat="41.747177" lon="-74.091711"/><trkpt lat="41.747217" lon="-74.091796"/><trkpt lat="41.747276" lon="-74.091867"/><trkpt lat="41.747336" lon="-74.091901"/><trkpt lat="41.747384" lon